WEBVTT

00:05.900 --> 00:12.190
The only person who can truly understand
your sadness and loneliness...

00:13.850 --> 00:14.820
...is me.

00:17.410 --> 00:18.370
Guys.

00:19.000 --> 00:20.850
Your smiles are fantastic.

00:21.260 --> 00:23.370
They are the signposts that light our way.

00:23.710 --> 00:24.580
Tokiya.

00:25.410 --> 00:27.880
But they're a lie?

00:29.810 --> 00:31.260
I'm disappointed.

00:31.860 --> 00:33.420
I trusted you.

00:34.020 --> 00:35.630
You're a liar.

00:36.260 --> 00:39.370
I can't believe you're even smiling now.

00:39.370 --> 00:41.430
I don't want to be around you anymore.

00:44.140 --> 00:47.350
What are you talking about? I...

00:48.940 --> 00:49.650
Nanami.

00:52.860 --> 00:55.320
Now let's sing together.

01:14.470 --> 01:17.050
Ittoki Otoya

01:21.470 --> 01:23.990
Otoya. Otoya!

01:25.310 --> 01:26.390
I can't.

01:26.390 --> 01:27.190
What?

01:27.190 --> 01:30.110
I'm sorry. I...

01:32.130 --> 01:33.500
...can't smile anymore.

01:34.110 --> 01:38.310
Otoya, are you all right?
What are you talking about?

01:38.720 --> 01:43.360
I can't be part of STARISH anymore.

01:44.130 --> 01:46.430
Otoya, what do you mean?

01:46.430 --> 01:47.250
Otoya?

01:46.430 --> 01:47.560
Ichinose Tokiya

01:53.210 --> 01:56.910
The number you have reached
is either powered off or...

01:59.990 --> 02:03.230
The number you have reached
is either powered off or...

03:48.390 --> 03:52.580
What did he mean by he can't
be part of STARISH anymore?

03:52.580 --> 03:54.000
I don't know.

03:54.000 --> 03:57.210
What does it mean that
he can't smile anymore?

03:57.210 --> 03:58.490
I don't know.

03:58.490 --> 04:00.010
Where is he?

04:00.010 --> 04:01.470
I don't know.

04:02.510 --> 04:04.610
He's not answering.

04:04.610 --> 04:06.260
What should we do?

04:06.650 --> 04:08.150
We have to find him.

04:08.880 --> 04:09.970
Excuse me.

04:10.950 --> 04:12.560
Is Ittoki-kun still missing?

04:12.560 --> 04:15.220
We still can't get in touch with him.

04:15.220 --> 04:16.400
Did something happen?

04:17.190 --> 04:19.070
Their song...

04:19.700 --> 04:20.360
Their song?

04:20.360 --> 04:24.910
A recording of their duet just arrived.

04:24.910 --> 04:26.440
A duet?

04:27.080 --> 04:28.700
What? You mean Otoya's?

04:28.700 --> 04:29.960
Yes.

04:29.960 --> 04:31.190
What do you mean?

04:31.920 --> 04:34.900
But didn't Otoya go on a trip
so he could work on the lyrics?

04:34.900 --> 04:35.540
Yes.

04:36.140 --> 04:38.960
But I just received an e-mail from Otori-san.

04:57.230 --> 05:02.550
Tear off that smiling mask

05:02.550 --> 05:07.730
You'll see a menacing and desolate world

05:07.730 --> 05:12.260
The sunflowers in the darkness

05:12.260 --> 05:20.990
Are torn to pieces as my song burns

05:13.200 --> 05:14.790
What?

05:26.450 --> 05:29.090
Is this Otoya?

05:33.420 --> 05:36.700
Was the song's concept
Otori Eiichi's suggestion?

05:36.700 --> 05:40.180
Yes. He wanted a soul-shaking song.

05:40.180 --> 05:42.270
Soul-shaking?

05:42.270 --> 05:46.700
He suggested a song that would release
the depths of a person's soul.

05:47.910 --> 05:51.450
No wonder he'd been acting
differently lately.

05:54.700 --> 05:57.530
But I can't believe he's not coming back.

05:58.170 --> 05:59.030
Why?

05:59.750 --> 06:02.000
Maybe something happened on his trip.

06:03.910 --> 06:04.670
Nanami-san.

06:06.860 --> 06:08.080
I have a request.

06:11.780 --> 06:14.770
Good. He's the best.

06:14.770 --> 06:19.390
It's rare for you to take
such a liking to someone.

06:21.670 --> 06:24.610
The trembling of my soul is still
running through my entire body.

06:28.490 --> 06:29.130
Nanami Haruka

06:29.130 --> 06:29.780
In Call

06:29.780 --> 06:30.610
Hello?

06:31.220 --> 06:32.660
This is Ichinose Tokiya.

06:34.070 --> 06:35.850
There's something I'd like to discuss.

06:39.920 --> 06:42.740
What do you want?

06:42.740 --> 06:44.170
Otoya won't come back.

06:45.740 --> 06:47.890
Do you have any ideas?

06:47.890 --> 06:49.430
Any ideas?

06:50.350 --> 06:52.970
His soul must still be trembling.

06:52.970 --> 06:53.510
What?

06:54.430 --> 06:56.840
He was exposed to the ultimate music.

06:57.360 --> 06:59.100
Coming down from that won't be quick.

07:00.250 --> 07:01.400
What did you do to him?

07:02.800 --> 07:07.320
I released the darkness in his soul
and made him show me his true self.

07:08.120 --> 07:09.450
His true self?

07:09.930 --> 07:17.340
You've lived with him for a long time,
but you don't know the truth about him.

07:19.850 --> 07:25.000
In the depths of Ittoki Otoya's heart
is a sunflower field of despair.

07:26.070 --> 07:28.960
A sunflower field of despair?

07:28.960 --> 07:31.720
It's splendid. It's exhilarating!

07:32.170 --> 07:35.750
We sang a song that shakes
the souls of those who hear it

07:35.750 --> 07:37.810
and stains them with the color of darkness.

07:40.860 --> 07:42.020
Excuse me.

07:45.230 --> 07:51.220
As one who doesn't possess the same soul,
you'll never understand how Otoya feels.

08:02.120 --> 08:05.980
His true self? A sunflower field of despair?

08:06.630 --> 08:09.840
You don't know the truth about him.

08:29.330 --> 08:31.900
Auntie. Hey, Auntie.

08:32.450 --> 08:33.570
It's a promise.

08:33.880 --> 08:37.120
When you get better,
let's go to the sunflower field together.

08:37.120 --> 08:40.670
Yes, we'll go to the sunflower field together.

08:41.700 --> 08:42.870
It's a promise.

08:42.870 --> 08:44.870
It's a promise.

08:53.340 --> 08:56.270
Poor thing. She was still so young.

08:56.270 --> 08:58.400
She was such a kind girl.

08:58.400 --> 09:02.130
She took in her nephew, Otoya-chan,
even though she was single.

09:02.130 --> 09:04.120
Must have been hard.

09:04.660 --> 09:06.930
It's my fault.

09:08.110 --> 09:11.530
If she hadn't taken me in, then Auntie...

09:15.260 --> 09:18.370
It's my fault.

09:37.830 --> 09:40.050
It's my fault.

09:51.410 --> 09:52.570
Well done.

09:53.050 --> 09:55.190
I knew you could do it, my son.

09:55.190 --> 09:56.820
What are you talking about?

09:57.430 --> 09:59.460
I heard the report.

09:59.460 --> 10:03.760
Apparently, Ittoki Otoya
hasn't returned home from his trip.

10:03.760 --> 10:06.990
I heard about that. What about it?

10:06.990 --> 10:12.210
So you knew. Everyone
in the industry is talking about it.

10:12.210 --> 10:15.390
Ittoki Otoya is missing.

10:15.390 --> 10:16.680
He's missing?

10:18.790 --> 10:22.600
Don't play dumb. Didn't you plan all of this?

10:23.440 --> 10:27.390
You gradually cornered him
and then suddenly went in for the kill.

10:27.390 --> 10:32.000
No. I was just pursuing the ultimate song.

10:32.000 --> 10:34.480
Well done, Eiichi!

10:41.410 --> 10:45.100
He's missing? I don't believe it.

10:49.860 --> 10:53.540
There's still no information?

10:53.540 --> 10:56.240
We're checking everyplace we can think of.

10:56.240 --> 10:58.050
But we can't find him.

11:01.400 --> 11:05.100
They're looking everywhere,
but they still can't find him.

11:07.750 --> 11:09.360
All we can do is wait.

11:09.360 --> 11:11.730
Otoya will come back.

11:12.430 --> 11:16.050
There's no objective evidence for it,
but I feel he will.

11:16.480 --> 11:18.600
They share a strong bond.

11:19.610 --> 11:21.030
You're right.

11:32.400 --> 11:35.430
Otoya never knew his father.

11:36.050 --> 11:38.800
He lost his mother before he could remember.

11:40.040 --> 11:42.720
His aunt raised him.

11:43.970 --> 11:47.090
But she passed away due to a serious illness.

11:47.640 --> 11:48.480
What?

11:48.480 --> 11:53.730
He felt it was his fault.

11:55.160 --> 11:57.280
It's my fault.

12:00.720 --> 12:06.870
By the time he arrived at the orphanage,
he may have thought

12:07.520 --> 12:11.520
that whatever was important to him,
he would someday lose.

12:13.100 --> 12:18.010
And apparently, he couldn't smile back then.

12:20.510 --> 12:21.970
No...

12:21.970 --> 12:23.030
Otoya.

12:23.540 --> 12:25.180
I had no idea.

12:25.180 --> 12:28.830
I can't believe Ikki had such emotional scars.

12:29.300 --> 12:32.600
I was told it was only when he was a child.

12:32.600 --> 12:39.320
So Otori Eiichi dug up old wounds
that he himself had forgotten.

12:39.320 --> 12:40.940
It's possible.

12:48.430 --> 12:50.990
You've lost a lot of things.

12:52.040 --> 12:57.590
Your father, your mother, the people
who raised you, a warm place to belong.

12:58.550 --> 13:02.300
Everything you wanted is gone.

13:04.350 --> 13:09.930
If I'm around, Nanami and STARISH will...

13:15.450 --> 13:20.980
Maybe Ikki thinks something
will happen to us if he stays.

13:20.980 --> 13:22.150
What?

13:23.680 --> 13:25.250
Why would he think that?

13:25.860 --> 13:27.760
We're friends.

13:27.760 --> 13:30.780
Why didn't he say something
to us before assuming that?

13:31.820 --> 13:35.040
It's not something that's easy to share, though.

13:35.040 --> 13:35.960
I know!

13:35.960 --> 13:39.080
But... but...

13:40.290 --> 13:41.840
He doesn't have to handle it on his own.

13:43.260 --> 13:44.570
Syo-kun.

13:46.390 --> 13:50.270
In any case, we need to find
him by tomorrow evening.

13:50.270 --> 13:50.640
What?

13:50.640 --> 13:52.300
The Song Festival.

13:52.300 --> 13:53.890
It's being broadcast live.

13:53.890 --> 13:59.020
That's right. If he's absent from
a live broadcast, it'll be a disaster.

13:59.330 --> 14:01.640
Tokiya, how can you be so calm?

14:01.640 --> 14:02.900
Yeah.

14:02.900 --> 14:06.400
Isn't Otoya more important
than work right now?

14:06.400 --> 14:08.190
He's not.

14:08.190 --> 14:12.470
If this gets out, Otoya will be hurt even more.

14:13.050 --> 14:14.080
That's why I'm saying this.

14:15.360 --> 14:16.530
Sorry.

14:16.530 --> 14:17.960
I'm sorry.

14:17.960 --> 14:20.210
No, I'm sorry.

14:24.640 --> 14:26.630
He's like me.

14:27.170 --> 14:31.910
I always thought that someday I had to
settle the score with my father,

14:31.910 --> 14:35.180
but for a long time I kept avoiding him.

14:35.180 --> 14:39.700
But when I returned home,
my father caught me off guard.

14:39.700 --> 14:41.440
I was at a loss.

14:42.410 --> 14:46.740
Ittoki must not know
what to do right now, either.

14:46.740 --> 14:52.740
Not only that, but it's his own heart
that he has to settle matters with.

14:54.610 --> 14:58.330
But I'm sure Otoya-kun will be fine.

15:00.000 --> 15:03.810
He can overcome his painful past.

15:04.310 --> 15:05.170
I was the same.

15:06.410 --> 15:09.800
With friends, we're stronger.

15:17.750 --> 15:20.580
You're right. I'm sure he'll be okay.

15:21.570 --> 15:25.690
I hope he remembers that he has us.

15:26.010 --> 15:29.400
I wish we could tell him how we feel.

15:29.400 --> 15:32.690
There must be a way.

15:33.570 --> 15:36.070
If we all think of a way
to tell Ittoki-kun how we feel,

15:36.610 --> 15:39.540
I'm sure we'll come up with something.

16:22.710 --> 16:24.450
You're alone.

16:25.030 --> 16:27.090
Face your true self.

16:32.660 --> 16:35.300
Happy Shining Day!

16:37.830 --> 16:40.640
Today is the anniversary of Shiny's debut.

16:40.970 --> 16:45.560
His rare hit single "For Love"
that exceeded twenty million

16:45.910 --> 16:49.610
in sales was his message of love.

16:49.610 --> 16:54.140
And his message was for those of you
out there pursuing your dreams

16:54.140 --> 16:57.120
who are on the verge of breaking.

16:57.910 --> 17:03.370
Even if you think you've lost something,
it's still hiding inside your heart.

17:03.370 --> 17:05.500
Like the sun above the clouds.

17:06.670 --> 17:09.340
Now listen to this song.

17:09.340 --> 17:11.340
It's a message from STARISH.

17:22.560 --> 17:28.050
You can always cry when you want to cry

17:28.050 --> 17:33.450
I'll hold you and your tears

17:33.450 --> 17:38.900
The sun always rises after the rain

17:38.900 --> 17:43.790
It will illuminate the map to the future

17:43.790 --> 17:49.890
We don't know what kind of story

17:49.890 --> 17:54.670
Waits at the end of this road

17:52.180 --> 17:54.670
...At the end of this road.

17:55.100 --> 18:00.300
There is no darkness the flames of hope

18:00.640 --> 18:05.020
Can't ever dispel

18:05.020 --> 18:06.630
We love us all

18:06.630 --> 18:08.100
We believe you

18:08.100 --> 18:10.900
You are who you are

18:08.100 --> 18:10.900
You are who you are.

18:10.900 --> 18:15.860
Paint your dreams as you see them

18:15.860 --> 18:17.200
We hold you

18:17.200 --> 18:18.860
We want you

18:18.860 --> 18:21.950
Let's go together, star love

18:21.950 --> 18:30.580
And we'll offer this symphony to you

18:31.880 --> 18:39.640
No matter what walls you run into

18:38.760 --> 18:42.930
Don't forget to smile

18:42.930 --> 18:50.140
Under love and stars and a rainbow of names

18:50.140 --> 18:57.840
As you pursue your dreams,
let your songs shine

19:08.900 --> 19:09.790
I want to see them.

19:10.540 --> 19:12.850
I want to see everyone.

19:23.180 --> 19:26.070
Did their message reach you?
We believe in you.

19:26.070 --> 19:27.060
And now...

19:27.060 --> 19:29.980
See you next time!

19:37.560 --> 19:38.560
I want to see them.

19:39.200 --> 19:40.450
I want to go home.

19:41.160 --> 19:44.650
But I can't. I still can't smile.

19:46.250 --> 19:49.770
I need to resolve this myself first.

20:18.560 --> 20:20.150
We're almost there.

20:34.820 --> 20:39.130
Auntie, I came to the sunflower field
we promised to visit.

20:40.260 --> 20:42.550
There aren't any flowers anymore, though.

20:43.570 --> 20:48.690
I'm sorry. I was afraid to think about you.

20:49.820 --> 20:53.520
I love you. I love you so much, but...

20:54.210 --> 20:59.360
I remember your smile
and your words so well, but...

21:00.430 --> 21:02.780
Otoya, no matter what happens,

21:02.780 --> 21:08.530
keep looking up and smiling
like the sunflowers I love.

21:09.000 --> 21:11.420
Even when you're sad, don't look down.

21:11.420 --> 21:14.640
The sun will always watch over you.

21:14.640 --> 21:17.460
Okay, but I'm not a sunflower.

21:18.110 --> 21:19.610
I'll be the sun.

21:19.610 --> 21:22.260
I'll shine down on you
with the smile of a sun.

21:22.750 --> 21:26.220
You're right. Keep smiling like the sun.

21:29.070 --> 21:30.840
I love you, Otoya.

21:31.550 --> 21:33.560
My dear Otoya.

21:41.700 --> 21:43.310
I'll do my best.

21:44.010 --> 21:48.390
I'll shine like the sun
and illuminate everyone as an idol.

21:49.240 --> 21:51.270
I'll make everyone smile.

21:52.200 --> 21:55.870
You just watch me, Auntie.

22:00.010 --> 22:00.830
Otoya.

24:06.250 --> 24:08.920
I believe in your bonds.

24:09.350 --> 24:10.300
Uta Pri.
